### MS3 — Soumissions (Arène)
### Deux modes d'utilisation :
###  - Script : python3 e2e/run_http_e2e.py exécute les requêtes 1 → 13 dans l'ordre
###    et ignore les blocs [SETUP].
###  - Manuel : exécuter d'abord les 3 blocs [SETUP] ci-dessous, puis n'importe quel endpoint.
### Les blocs [SETUP] créent les soumissions et alimentent {{submissionId}}, {{submissionIdB}}
### et {{lateSubmissionId}}. Sans eux, ces variables gardent leur valeur temporaire
### (aaaa/bbbb/cccc) et un endpoint avec {{...}} répond 404.
### Attention : [SETUP] crée des brouillons. Pour GET/PUT verdict, exécuter d'abord 4 (submit),
### puis 5 (verdict) sur {{submissionId}} ; pour 10/11/12, exécuter 9 puis 10 sur {{submissionIdB}}.
### Pour passer par la gateway : remplacer @host par http://localhost:8080/ms3
### Attention : le bloc "> {% ... %}" est un script de réponse, jamais une partie du corps JSON.

@host = http://localhost:8083
@api = {{host}}/api/submissions
@challengeId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@applicantId = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@submissionId = aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa
@submissionIdB = bbbbbbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb
@lateSubmissionId = cccccccc-cccc-cccc-cccc-cccccccccccc
@deadline = 2030-12-31T23:59:59

### [SETUP] A — créer la soumission principale (manuel avant tout endpoint) — 201
POST {{api}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}",
  "applicantId": "{{applicantId}}",
  "repoUrl": "https://github.com/example/arena-solution.git",
  "branch": "main"
}

> {%
client.global.set("submissionId", response.body.id);
%}

### [SETUP] B — créer la 2e soumission (manuel) — 201
POST {{api}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}",
  "applicantId": "44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444",
  "repoUrl": "https://github.com/example/arena-solution-2.git",
  "branch": "feature/optimize"
}

> {%
client.global.set("submissionIdB", response.body.id);
%}

### [SETUP] C — créer la soumission pour le test de retard (manuel) — 201
POST {{api}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}",
  "applicantId": "55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555",
  "repoUrl": "https://github.com/example/arena-late.git",
  "branch": "main"
}

> {%
client.global.set("lateSubmissionId", response.body.id);
%}

### 1. Créer une soumission (brouillon) — 201
POST {{api}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}",
  "applicantId": "{{applicantId}}",
  "repoUrl": "https://github.com/example/arena-solution.git",
  "branch": "main"
}

> {%
client.global.set("submissionId", response.body.id);
%}

### 2. Lister les soumissions du défi — 200
GET {{api}}?challengeId={{challengeId}}
Accept: application/json

### 2b. Lister filtré par statut — 200
GET {{api}}?challengeId={{challengeId}}&status=SUBMITTED
Accept: application/json

### 3. Détail d'une soumission — 200
GET {{api}}/{{submissionId}}
Accept: application/json

### 4. Soumettre définitivement (fige le commit) — 200, puis 409 si déjà soumise
POST {{api}}/{{submissionId}}/submit?commitSha=abc1234&deadline={{deadline}}
Accept: application/json

### 5. Déposer le verdict (appel interne MS5) — 200
PUT {{api}}/{{submissionId}}/verdict
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "submissionId": "{{submissionId}}",
  "result": "PASS",
  "passed": 8,
  "failed": 2,
  "total": 10,
  "coverage": 87.5,
  "logsUrl": "https://ci.example.com/builds/42/logs"
}

### 6. Lire le verdict — 200 (404 avant le dépôt du verdict)
GET {{api}}/{{submissionId}}/verdict
Accept: application/json

### Erreur : soumission introuvable — 404
GET {{api}}/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/json

### Erreur : verdict introuvable — 404
GET {{api}}/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/verdict
Accept: application/json

### Erreur : passed + failed ≠ total — 409
PUT {{api}}/{{submissionId}}/verdict
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "submissionId": "{{submissionId}}",
  "result": "FAIL",
  "passed": 3,
  "failed": 3,
  "total": 10,
  "coverage": 42.0,
  "logsUrl": "https://ci.example.com/builds/43/logs"
}

### Erreur : identifiant du verdict différent de l'URL — 409
PUT {{api}}/{{submissionId}}/verdict
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "submissionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "result": "PASS",
  "passed": 10,
  "failed": 0,
  "total": 10,
  "coverage": 100.0,
  "logsUrl": "https://ci.example.com/builds/44/logs"
}

### 7. Créer une 2e soumission (autre candidat, branche feature) — 201
POST {{api}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}",
  "applicantId": "44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444",
  "repoUrl": "https://github.com/example/arena-solution-2.git",
  "branch": "feature/optimize"
}

> {%
client.global.set("submissionIdB", response.body.id);
%}

### 8. Lister les brouillons du défi — 200
GET {{api}}?challengeId={{challengeId}}&status=DRAFT
Accept: application/json

### 9. Soumettre la 2e soumission (commit figé, deadline future) — 200
POST {{api}}/{{submissionIdB}}/submit?commitSha=deadbeef&deadline={{deadline}}
Accept: application/json

### 10. Déposer un verdict FAIL sur la 2e soumission — 200 (statut final REJECTED)
PUT {{api}}/{{submissionIdB}}/verdict
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "submissionId": "{{submissionIdB}}",
  "result": "FAIL",
  "passed": 4,
  "failed": 6,
  "total": 10,
  "coverage": 61.5,
  "logsUrl": "https://ci.example.com/builds/43/logs"
}

### 11. Vérifier le statut final REJECTED — 200
GET {{api}}/{{submissionIdB}}
Accept: application/json

### 12. Lister les soumissions REJECTED du défi — 200
GET {{api}}?challengeId={{challengeId}}&status=REJECTED
Accept: application/json

### 13. Créer une soumission pour le test de retard — 201
POST {{api}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}",
  "applicantId": "55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555",
  "repoUrl": "https://github.com/example/arena-late.git",
  "branch": "main"
}

> {%
client.global.set("lateSubmissionId", response.body.id);
%}

### Erreur : soumission hors délai — 409
POST {{api}}/{{lateSubmissionId}}/submit?commitSha=toolate&deadline=2020-01-01T00:00:00
Accept: application/json

### Erreur : double soumission (commit déjà figé) — 409
POST {{api}}/{{submissionId}}/submit?commitSha=anothercommit&deadline={{deadline}}
Accept: application/json

### Erreur : verdict sur un brouillon non soumis — 409
PUT {{api}}/{{lateSubmissionId}}/verdict
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "submissionId": "{{lateSubmissionId}}",
  "result": "PASS",
  "passed": 10,
  "failed": 0,
  "total": 10,
  "coverage": 100.0,
  "logsUrl": "https://ci.example.com/builds/45/logs"
}

### Liste vide pour un défi inconnu — 200 []
GET {{api}}?challengeId=99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999
Accept: application/json

### Erreur : champ obligatoire manquant (repoUrl) — 400
POST {{api}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}",
  "applicantId": "66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666666",
  "branch": "main"
}

### Actuator — état de santé détaillé (db, diskSpace, discoveryClient, ping) — 200
GET {{host}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

### Actuator — informations de l'application — 200
GET {{host}}/actuator/info
Accept: application/json

### Actuator — liste des métriques disponibles — 200
GET {{host}}/actuator/metrics
Accept: application/json

### Actuator — détail d'une métrique (temps de réponse HTTP) — 200
GET {{host}}/actuator/metrics/http.server.requests
Accept: application/json

### Actuator — santé du serveur Eureka — 200
GET http://localhost:8761/actuator/health
Accept: application/json
